#* {{quote-journal|en|passage=But what sight is that? It seems a town right in the river, each building standing upon its own foundation, with the deep, '''strong''' current of the river sweeping all around it? They are flouring mills operated by the natural current of the stream.|title=Notes from Hungary|work=The Michigan Farmer|date=April 1853|author=Warren Isham|editor=Warren Isham|issue=4|volume=XI|titleurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Michigan_Farmer/8iZDoaHe4RMC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA98}}
