#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Proverbs|chapter=24|verse=5|passage=A wise man is '''strong''', yea a man of knowledge [[encreaseth]] strength.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Two Towers|passage=Perhaps we grows very '''strong''', '''stronger''' than Wraiths. Lord Smeagol? Gollum the Great? The Gollum! Eat fish every day, three times a day, fresh from the sea.|year=1954|author=J[ohn] R[onald] R[euel] Tolkien|page=619|year_published=2001|authorlink=J. R. R. Tolkien|chapter=The Passage of the Marshes|series=The Lord of the Rings|seriesvolume=2|publisher=HarperCollinsPublishers}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2010|Heinrich D Holland, Karl K. Turekian|Isotope Geochemistry|text=Outgassing of oxygen is '''strongest''' when primary production rates are greatest; ingassing is at a maximum during net respiration.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=May 27, 2007|author=Sam Roberts|title=In a City Known for Its Renters, a Record Number Now Own Their Homes|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/27/nyregion/27owners.html
|passage=“Homeownership,” says John H. Mollenkopf, executive director of the Center for Urban Research at the City University of New York Graduate Center, “is the '''strongest''' predictor of being likely to turn out in local politics and being a bit more conservative and antitax in your general outlook.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210227064046/https://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/27/nyregion/27owners.html}}
