===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|sort}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|kynde|id=nature}}, {{m|enm|kinde}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cynd}}, {{m|ang|ġecynd|t=inherent nature, disposition, kind, gender, generation, race}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kundi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kinþiz}}, related to {{m+|gem-pro|*kunją|t=race, kin}} and {{cog|ang|cennan|t=to bear, give birth}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|goh|gikunt|t=nature, kind}}, {{cog|is|kind|t=race, species, kind}}. {{doublet|en|gens|genesis|jati}}. See also {{m|en|kin}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|kinde|kynd|kynde||obsolete}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[type]], [[race]] or [[category]]; a group of entities that have common characteristics such that they may be grouped together.
#: {{ux|en|What '''kind''' of person are you?}}
#: {{ux|en|What '''kind''' of ice-cream would you like? There's chocolate, strawberry{{,}} and lemon.}}
#: {{ux|en|Neither of them is the marrying '''kind'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=III|canto=V|stanza=1|passage=How diversely Love doth his pageants play, / And shews his powre in variable '''kinds''' !}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=1|passage=“{{...}} the awfully hearty sort of Christmas cards that people do send to other people that they don't know at all well. You know. The '''kind''' that have mottoes like<br/><small>&nbsp; Here's rattling good luck and roaring good cheer, / With lashings of food and great hogsheads of beer. {{...}}</small>”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|title=Material Objects in Confucian and Aristotelian Metaphysics|author=James Dominic Rooney|page=166|passage=That in virtue of which all of his material parts are of the same '''kind''' ''human being'' is what makes those parts belong to Hook, but Hook is neither identical with his '''kind''' (the essence of ''human being''), nor is Hook merely that which makes him a member of the '''kind''' or all his parts human (his soul).}}
# A [[makeshift]] or otherwise [[atypical]] specimen.
#: {{ux|en|The opening served as a '''kind''' of window.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Huckleberry Finn|chapter=VIII|passage=I got my traps out of the canoe and made me a nice camp in the thick woods. I made a '''kind''' of a tent out of my blankets to put my things under so the rain couldn't get at them.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} One's inherent [[nature]]; [[character]], natural disposition.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1533|title=The second parte of the confutacion of Tyndals answere in whyche is also confuted the chyrche that Tyndale deuyseth|author=Thomas More|page=|passage=Must yt nedes folowe that theyr fayth was chaunged in '''kynde''', bycause yt was augmented in degrees.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1551|title=The rule of reason, conteinyng the arte of logique|author=Thomas Wilson|page=|passage=The generall woorde, is spoken of many, that differ either in '''kynd''', or els in nombre.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1665|title=Occasional Reflections upon Several Subjects. Whereto is premis'd a Discourse about such kind of thoughts|author=Robert Boyle|page=|passage='Tis all one..whether our Afflictions be the same with those of others, in '''Kind''', or not Superiour to them in Degree.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|title=Animal Rights|author=D. DeGrazia|page=|passage=He also argued powerfully, if less influentially, that animals' and humans' capacities differ largely in degree and not in '''kind'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[family|Family]], [[lineage]].
#* "She Moved through the Fair" (traditional Irish folk song)
#*: My young love said to me, My mother won’t mind<br/>And my father won’t slight you for your lack of '''kind'''.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[manner|Manner]].
# {{senseid|en|payment}} Goods or services used as payment, as in [[barter]].
#: {{coi|en|[[in kind|in '''kind''']]|with goods or services instead of with money}}
#: {{ux|en|I don't have any money but I can pay in '''kind''' by washing the dishes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1691|author=w:John Dryden|title=Prologue to {{w|King Arthur (opera)|King Arthur}}
|passage=Some of you, on pure instinct of nature, / Are led by '''kind''' t'admire your fellow-creature.}}
# Equivalent [[means]] used as [[response]] to an action.
