===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

[[File:Cross-Pattee-Heraldry.svg|thumb|150px|[[cross pattée|'''Cross''' pattée]]]]

[[File:CrocefissioneRaffaello.jpg|thumb|150px|An artist's depiction of Jesus being executed on a '''cross''']]
[[File:Boysenberry.jpg|150px|thumb|A boysenberry – a '''cross''' between several other berries]]
[[File:CFOP-Cross_solved.png|thumb|250px|The '''cross''', one of the steps in a popular algorithm for solving the Rubik's Cube]]

# {{senseid|en|geometrical figure involving intersecting lines}} A geometrical figure consisting of two straight [[line]]s or [[bar]]s [[intersecting]] each other such that at least one of them is [[bisect]]ed by the other.
#: {{cot|en|q1=similar shapes|tee|T|t|;|ex|x|;|chi#Noun|mul:χ|q8=marks meaning yes or no|tick|check|checkmark|❎|❌}}
#: {{ux|en|Put a '''cross''' for a wrong answer and a tick for a right one.}}
# {{senseid|en|heraldry}} {{lb|en|heraldry}} Any geometric figure having this or a similar shape, such as a [[cross of Lorraine]] or a [[Maltese cross]].
#: {{hyper|en|charge<id:heraldry>}}
#: {{hypo|en|cross flory|cross crosslet|cross moline|cross pattée|cross bottony|''see [[w:Crosses_in_heraldry#Named_variants|others]]''}}
# {{senseid|en|execution device}} A [[wooden]] [[post]] with a [[perpendicular]] [[beam]] attached and used (especially in the Roman Empire) to [[execute]] [[criminal]]s (by [[crucifixion]]).
#: {{syn|en|crucifix<id:execution device>}}
#: {{cot|en|gibbet#Noun|gallows<id:execution device, for hanging>}}
#: {{ux|en|Criminals were commonly executed on a wooden '''cross'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|Cross, Crucifix, of Jesus Christ}} {{lb|en|Christianity}} {{alternative case form of|en|Cross|t=the [[crucifix|Crucifix]], the cross on which [[Christ]] was [[crucify|crucified]]}}.
#: {{cot|en|q1=as a symbol or emoji|✝|☦<qq:Eastern Orthodoxy>}}
#: {{l|en|True Cross}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Don Roderick|stanza=XXVII|page=31|passage=From the dim landscape roll the clouds away— / The Christians have regained their heritage; / Before the '''Cross''' has waned the Crescent's ray, / And many a monastery decks the stage, / And lofty church, and low-brow'd hermitage.}}
# {{lb|en|Christianity}} A hand [[gesture]] made in [[imitation]] of the shape of the [[Cross]]; [[sign of the cross]].
#: {{syn|en|sign of the cross}}
#: {{ux|en|She made the '''cross''' after swearing.}}
# {{senseid|en|any representation of the Crucifix of Jesus, e.g., pendant, adornment}} {{lb|en|Christianity}} Any representation of the [[crucifix]], as in religious architecture, burial markers, jewelry, etc.
#: {{syn|en|crucifix<id:any representation of the Crucifix of Jesus, e.g., pendant, adornment>}}
#: {{ux|en|She was wearing a '''cross''' on her necklace.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|from Christ's bearing of the cross}} A [[difficult]] [[situation]] that must be [[endure]]d.
#: {{ux|en|It's a '''cross''' I must bear.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1641|author=w:Ben Jonson|title=Timber| passage=Heaven prepares good men with '''crosses'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=w:You Oughta Know|album=w:Jagged Little Pill|artist=w:Alanis Morissette|year=1995|passage=It's not fair to deny me / Of the '''cross''' I bear that you gave to me / You, you, you oughta know}}
# The act of going across; the act of passing from one side to the other
#: {{ux|en|A quick '''cross''' of the road.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} An animal or plant produced by [[crossbreeding]] or [[cross-fertilization]].
#: {{syn|en|hybrid}}
# One element of a hybrid species or type.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1869|author={{w|Alfred Russel Wallace}}|title={{w|The Malay Archipelago}}|publisher=Macmillan and Co.|year_published=|volume=I|location=London|page=471|passage=The native Amboynese who reside in the city are a strange half-civilized, half-savage lazy people, who seem to be a mixture of at least three races - Portuguese, Malay, and Papuan or Ceramese, with an occasional '''cross''' of Chinese or Dutch.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[hybrid]] of any kind.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1856|author=w:Lord Dufferin|title=w:Letters from High Latitudes|passage=Toning down the ancient Viking into a sort of a '''cross''' between Paul Jones and Jeremy Diddler}}
# {{lb|en|boxing}} A [[hook]] thrown over the opponent's [[punch]].
# {{lb|en|football}} A [[pass]] in which the ball is kicked from a side of the [[pitch]] to a position close to the [[opponent]]’s [[goal]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2010| author=Chris Whyatt| title=Chelsea 1 - 0 Bolton| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm| passage=And Stamford Bridge erupted with joy as Florent Malouda slotted in a '''cross''' from Drogba, who had stayed just onside.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260204040745/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm|archivedate=4 February 2026}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Leander Schaerlaeckens|title=Deniz Undav’s double earns Germany dramatic late win against Côte d’Ivoire|date=2026-06-20|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/20/germany-cote-divoire-group-e-match-report|passage=More German peril would follow as Joshua Kimmich swung in a '''cross''' for Havertz, whose well-placed header was majestically saved by Yahia Fofana.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013064325/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jun/20/germany-cote-divoire-group-e-match-report|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
# A place where [[road]]s intersect and lead off in four directions; a [[crossroad]] (common in UK and Irish place names such as ''Gerrards Cross'').
# A monument that marks such a place. (Also common in UK or Irish place names such as ''Charing Cross'')
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[coin]] stamped with the figure of a cross, or that side of such a piece on which the cross is stamped; hence, money in general.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|act=II|scene=iv|passage=I should bear no '''cross''' if I did bear you; for I think you have no money in your purse.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|Ireland}} Church lands.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1612|author={{w|John Davies (poet)|John Davies}}|title=Discoverie of the True Causes why Ireland was never entirely subdued
|passage=the church-lands lying within the same, which were called the '''Cross'''}}
# A [[line]] across or through another line.
# {{lb|en|surveying}} An instrument for laying of offsets perpendicular to the main course.
# A pipe-fitting with four branches whose [[axis|axes]] usually form a [[right angle]].
# {{lb|en|Rubik's Cube}} Four edge [[cubie]]s of one side that are in their right places, forming the shape of a cross.
# {{lb|en|cartomancy}} The thirty-sixth [[Lenormand]] card.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[betrayal]]; dishonest practices, especially deliberately losing a sporting contest. <!--Chambers 1908-->
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[crossfire|Crossfire]].

