left.content:
{{also|lëft}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewbʰ-|id=cut off}}
From {{inh|en|enm|left}}, {{m|enm|luft}}, {{m|enm|leoft}}, {{m|enm|lift}}, {{m|enm|lyft}}, from {{inh|en|ang|left}}, {{m|ang|lyft|t=weak, clumsy, foolish}}, attested in {{cog|ang|lyftādl|t=palsy, paralysis}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*luft-}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*lubjaną|t=to castrate, lop off}} (compare dialectal {{cog|en|lib}}, {{cog|fy|lobje}}, {{cog|nl|lubben}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)lewp-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)lup-|t=hanging limply}}. Compare {{cog|sco|left|t=left}}, {{cog|frr|lefts}}, {{m|frr|leeft}}, {{m|frr|leefts|t=left}}, {{cog|fy|lofts|t=left}}, obsolete {{cog|nl|lucht}}, {{m|nl|leftsch}}, {{m|nl|lefts}}, {{m|nl|lefs|t=left}}, dialectal {{cog|nl|loof|t=weak, worthless}}, archaic {{cog|nds|lucht|t=left}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{sense|political left}} {{l|en|Left}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛft/|a=RP,IE}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɫɛft/|a=GA}}
*: {{audio|en|En-uk-left.ogg|a=RP}}
*: {{audio|en|En-us-left.ogg|a=GA}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛf/|/ˈlɛfʔ/|a=Dublin}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛft|s=1}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|further,more,er|sup=furthest,most,~most,est}}
<!-- lefter: "the lefter side of the debate"--Dina Cappiello, Associated Press-->
<!-- most left: "from one (the most left or liberal) to zero" --Jack Vowles, Voters' Veto: The 2002 Election in New Zealand (2004) -->

# Designating the side of the body toward the [[west]] when one is facing [[north]]; the side of the body on which the [[heart]] is located in most humans; the opposite of [[right]]. This [[arrow]] points to the reader's left: ←
#: {{syn|en|sinister|sinistral}}
#: {{ant|en|right|dexter|dextral}}
#: {{par|en|port}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''left''' side.}}
# [[anticlockwise|Anticlockwise]], particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation.
#: {{ux|en|The road up ahead contains a '''left''' bend.}}
#: {{ux|en|Rotate the bolt to the '''left''' to loosen it.}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} Designating the bank of a river (etc.) on one's left when facing downstream (i.e. facing forward while floating with the current); that is, the north bank of a river that flows eastward. If this arrow: ⥲ shows the direction of the current, the tilde is on the left side of the river.
#: {{ux|en|The Eiffel Tower is on the '''left''' bank of the [[Seine]].}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=March 23, 1904
|origdate=March 22, 1904
|quotee={{w|Yevgeni Ivanovich Alekseyev|Viceroy Alexieff}}
|title=Waiting for the First Collision in the Yalu Region
|journal=w:St. Louis Post-Dispatch
|url=https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_st-louis-post-dispatch_1904-03-23_56_215/
|location=St. Louis
|volume=56
|issue=215
|issn=1930-9600
|oclc=1764810
|page=2
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/per_st-louis-post-dispatch_st-louis-post-dispatch_1904-03-23_56_215/page/n1/
|column=2
|text=The following dispatch has been received from Viceroy Alexieff, dated Mukden, March 22:<br>“Gen. Mitchenkow reports that on March 17 our scouts approached Anju and observed on the '''left''' bank of the Ching Chong river, opposite Anju, retrenchments made by the enemy.}}
# {{lb|en|politics}} [[left-wing|Left-wing]]; pertaining to the political left.
#: {{ant|en|right}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1941|author=w:George Orwell|title={{w|The Lion and the Unicorn: Socialism and the English Genius|The Lion and the Unicorn}}
|passage=It should be noted that there is now no [[intelligentsia]] that is not in some sense "'''Left'''". Perhaps the last [[right-wing]] [[intellectual]] was {{w|T. E. Lawrence}}. Since about 1930 everyone describable as an “[[intellectual]]” has lived in a state of chronic discontent with the existing order.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1949|author={{w|Friedrich Hayek|F. A. Hayek}}|title=The Intellectuals and Socialism|journal={{w|University of Chicago Law Review}}|publisher={{w|University of Chicago}}|location={{w|Chicago}}|volume=16|number=3|doi=10.2307/1597903|page=422|passage=Who does not know the practical man who in his own field denounces socialism as "pernicious rot" but when he steps outside his subject spouts socialism like any '''left''' journalist.}}
# {{lb|en|syntax}} Relating to the beginning or earlier part of a phrase.
#: {{ux|en|'''left''' dislocation}}

[[File:Two_angelcots.jpg|thumb|The fruit to the viewer's '''left''' is smaller.]]

