# {{lb|en|informal|uncommon}} Causing thirst; giving one a need to drink.
#: {{ux|en|Marching is '''thirsty''' work.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|author=Bram Stoker|title=Dracula|passage=I had for dinner, or rather supper, a chicken done up some way with red pepper, which was very good but '''thirsty'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Charlotte Williamson|title=Vehicle maintenance for women|passage=Invest in a water bottle: cycling can be '''thirsty''' work.|isbn=9781740454759}}
# {{senseid|en|craving something immaterial}} {{lb|en|figurative}} [[crave|Craving]] something immaterial.
#: {{syn|en|athirst<q:archaic>}}
#: {{co|en|'''thirsty''' for knowledge}}
#: {{co|en|'''thirsty''' for attention}}
#: {{ux|en|After the president left office, the nation was '''thirsty''' for change.}}
