===Etymology 3===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰrun-}}
Possibly either:<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|id=260304|date=March 2022}}</ref>

* a {{glossary|blend}} of Shetland {{der|en|sco|nune|t=to sing softly, croon, hum}} (from {{der|en|da|nynne}}, {{der|en|no|nuna}}, {{m|no|nynna|t=to hum; to sing}}, originally {{glossary|imitative}})<ref>{{R:Dictionary of the Scots Language|entry=nune|pos=''v.'', ''n.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|url=https://dsl.ac.uk/entry/snd/nune_v_n2|source=SND}}</ref> + {{m+|en|doodle|w=1|t=to play the bagpipes}} {{qualifier|chiefly Scotland}}; or
* from {{der|en|nrn|-}} (unattested), from {{der|en|non|*grynta}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*grunnatjaną|t=to grunt}}, a {{glossary|frequentative}} of {{der|en|gem-pro|*grunnōną|t=to grunt}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰrun-|t=to shout}} (and thus a {{doublet|en|grunt|nocap=1}}).

