#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=159|volume=II|passage=Scenes, long since forgotten, had been '''peopling''' his solitude with one still cherished image paramount over all; one young fair face, whose sweet eyes seemed to look upon him reproachfully:...}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become [[populous]] or [[populated]].
# {{senseid|en|inhabit}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[inhabit]]; to [[occupy]]; to [[populate]].
#* {{ante|1645}}, [[w:John Milton|John Milton]], ''[[s:Il Penseroso|Il Penseroso]]'', lines 7–8:
