kitchen.content:
{{also|Kitchen}}
==English==
{{wp|lang=en|+ (disambiguation)}}
{{swp|lang=en}}
{{commonscat|Kitchens}}
[[File:Modern Kitchen.jpg|right|thumb|A modern '''kitchen'''.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|kitchin||archaic}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|kichene}}, {{m|enm|kichen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cyċen}}, {{m|ang|cyċene}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kukinā}}, a borrowing from {{der|en|la-lat|cocīna}}, from earlier {{m|la|coquīna|t=kitchen; cuisine}}, from {{m|la|coquō||to cook}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-||to cook, become ripe}}.

In other languages, the cognate term often refers both to the room and the type of cooking. In English, the distinction is generally made via the etymological twins {{m|en|kitchen||room}} (Latin via Germanic) and {{doublet|en|cuisine|t1=type of cooking|notext=1}} (Latin via {{cog|fr|-}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪt͡ʃ(ɪ)n/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-kitchen.ogg|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪt͡ʃ(ə)n/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-kitchen.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪtʃɪn|ɪtʃən|s=2}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkit͡ʃin/|a=SG}}
* {{hyphenation|en|kit|chen}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q43164}}A [[room]] or area for preparing food.
#: {{ux|en|We cook in the '''kitchen'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Foreword|passage=Everything a living animal could do to destroy and to desecrate bed and walls had been done. {{...}}&nbsp; A canister of flour from the '''kitchen''' had been thrown at the looking-glass and lay like trampled snow over the remains of a decent blue suit with the lining ripped out which lay on top of the ruin of a plastic wardrobe.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=Jona Lewie; Keef Trouble|title=You'll Always Find Me in the Kitchen at Parties|year=1980|artist=w:Jona Lewie|passage=I always leave the stuff piled up, piled up in the sink / But you will always find him in the '''kitchen''' at parties}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} [[cuisine|Cuisine]]; style of cooking.
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2011 |title=Essential Pépin: More Than 700 All-Time Favorites from My Life in Food|author=Jacques Pépin |page=|ISBN=0547607385|passage=I had been trained with the rigidity and discipline of the French '''kitchen''', and now I was embracing American informality.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2011 |title=Paradise Kitchen: Caribbean Cooking with Chef Daniel Orr |author=Daniel Orr |page=221|ISBN=0253356083|passage=My palate passionately lies in the savory '''kitchen''' with its salty fats and infernal flavors of chilies and spices.}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2015|title=Falafel Nation: Cuisine and the Making of National Identity in Israel|author=Yael Raviv |page=|ISBN=0803290233|passage=Kline wrote that, according to various recent surveys, the young Israeli-born generation generally preferred a Mediterranean diet and dishes from the “Oriental” '''kitchen'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2015|title=1,000 Foods To Eat Before You Die: A Food Lover's Life List |author=Mimi Sheraton |page=651|ISBN=076118306X|passage=Named for the La Merced monastery, which was built in 1594 and on whose grounds the market is now located, it is just east of Mexico City's famed Zócalo plaza and is a must-visit for anyone wanting to experience the many delectable specialties of the Mexican '''kitchen'''.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|African American Vernacular English}} The [[nape]] of a person's [[hairline]], often referring to its uncombed or "nappy" look.
# {{lb|en|music}} The [[percussion]] section of an [[orchestra]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|author=Norman Del Mar|title=Anatomy of the Orchestra|passage=For obvious reasons the percussion is normally arranged along the back of the platform, whether centrally or to one side, and sometimes also in two tiers, the heavy, noisier instruments behind, and the pitched, agile instruments such as vibraphone, marimba, etc. in front. An outstanding exception, however, exists in Roberto Gerhard's ''Epithalamion'' where the composer expressly desired that the all-important '''kitchen''' department be spread out in front of the strings and hence nearest the audience.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[utensil]] for [[roast]]ing [[meat]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|title=The Warm Springs Receipt-book|page=70
|passage=There are two modes of roasting: One is to use a tin '''kitchen''' before an open fire, and the other, and more common way, is to use a hot oven.}}
# {{lb|en|attributive}} A [[domesticated]] or [[uneducated]] form of a language.
#* {{RQ:Haggard King Solomon's Mines|passage=Sir Henry and Umbopo sat conversing in a mixture of broken English and '''kitchen''' Zulu, in low voices, but earnestly enough.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[public]] [[gaming]] [[room]] in a [[casino]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1925|author=William Rutherford Hayes Trowbridge|title=In the sun with a passport|page=31
|passage=Having done what was required to gain admittance to the "'''kitchen'''," as the public rooms are termed, as well as to the more exclusive "Salle Privée" {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Fleming Casino Royale|passage=But on this June evening when Bond walked through the ''''kitchen'''' into the salle privée, it was with a sensation of confidence and cheerful anticipation that he changed a million francs into plaques of fifty mille and took a seat {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Anything eaten as a [[relish]] with bread, potatoes, etc.; a [[condiment]].
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Kidnapped|passage=“They,” said he, meaning the collops, “are such as I gave his Royal Highness in this very house; bating the lemon juice, for at that time we were glad to get the meat and never fashed for '''kitchen'''. Indeed, there were mair dragoons than lemons in my country in the year forty-six.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1890|author=w:Joseph Jacobs|title=s:English Fairy Tales|chapter=The Red Ettin|page=136
|passage=Snouk but and snouk ben, / I find the smell of an earthly man; / Be he living, or be he dead, / His heart shall be '''kitchen''' to my bread.}}
# The region of a [[billiard table]] between the head rail and the head string.

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|area for preparing food}} A {{m|en||kitchen [[fruit]]}}, {{m|en||kitchen [[apple]]}}, or the like, or one {{m|en||good for the kitchen}}, is one suitable for use in prepared foods.

