#* {{quote-book|en|year=1830|title=The Imperial Magazine |author= |page= |ISBN= |passage=His Maker has not so endowed him as to lay him under the necessity of '''kitchening''', so to speak, a slender share of talent, and, by rigid economy, make it go as far as possible. }}
