===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:birthdai<ety:inh<ang:ġebyrddæġ>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|birthdai}}, {{m|enm|birtheday}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġebyrddæġ|t=birthday}}, influenced by {{cog|non|burðr}}, equivalent to {{com|en|birth|day}}. Compare {{cog|stq|Gebuursdai|t=birthday}}, {{cog|nl|geboortedag|t=birthday}}, {{cog|nds|Geboortsdag|t=birthday}}, {{cog|de|Geburtstag|t=birthday}}, {{cog|no|bursdag}}, {{m|no|gebursdag|t=birthday}}. Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|nativitee|t=birth, nativity, birthday}}, from {{noncog|fro|nativité}}, {{m|fro|nativited}}, from {{noncog|la|nātīvitas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɜːθ.deɪ/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɜːθ.dei/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-birthday.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|bûrthʹdā'|a=US,Canada}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbɝθˌdeɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-birthday.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)θdeɪ|ɜːθdɪ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[anniversary]] of the day on which someone is born. {{defdate|from 1570s}}
#: {{syn|en|natal day<l:archaic>}}
#: {{ux|en|When's your '''birthday'''? Mine's on April 1.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll be thirty-seven (years old) next '''birthday'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|My fortieth '''birthday''' is only two years off!}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Oliver Twist|chapter=2|text=Oliver Twist's ninth '''birthday''' found him a pale thin child, somewhat diminutive in stature, and decidedly small in circumference.}}
#* '''1903''', [[w:L. Frank Baum|L. Frank Baum]], ''[[s:The Surprising Adventures of the Magical Monarch of Mo and His People/Chapter 5|The Surprising Adventures of the Magical Monarch of Mo and His People]]'', The Fifth Surprise: The Monarch Celebrates His '''Birthday''',
#*: One of the Wise Men said the King was born in February; another declared it was in May, and a third figured the great event happened in October. So the King issued a royal decree that he should have three '''birthdays''' every year, in order to be on the safe side; and whenever he happened to think of it he put in an odd '''birthday''' or two for luck.
#* '''1906''', [[w:Edith Nesbit|Edith Nesbit]], ''[[s:The Railway Children/Chapter 9|The Railway Children]]'', Chapter 9: The pride of Perks,
#*: "And we thought we'd make a nice '''birthday''' for him. He's been so awfully jolly decent to us, you know, Mother," said Peter, "and we agreed that next bun-day we'd ask you if we could."
#* {{circa|1911}}, [[w:Cotton Mather|Cotton Mather]], [[w:Worthington Chauncey Ford|Worthington Chauncey Ford]] (editor), ''Diary of Cotton Mather'', Volume 1: 1681-1708, footnote, [http://books.google.com/books?id=i0M-AAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1&dq=%22birthday|birthdays%22&hl=en&ei=1exYTre8OayHmQXxqdyjDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CEYQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=%22birthday|birthdays%22&f=false page 1],
#*: It was his custom to begin a new year's record on February 12, his '''birthday'''.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 4 1921|title=[[s:The Times/1921/News/Birthday Honours — Companions of Honour|Birthday Honours — Companions of Honour]]|journal=w:The Times
|passage=The King's '''Birthday''', which occurred yesterday, will be officially observed to-day, and the customary list of honours conferred on the occasion is published.}}
# The anniversary of the day on which something is created.
# The date on which someone is born or something is created, more commonly called {{m|en|birthdate}} or {{m|en|date of birth}}.
# A [[birthday party]].
#: {{ux|en|I'd like to invite you all to my '''birthday'''.}}

